<title>INDIA: India's LML says 95/96 net lower.</title>
<headline>India's LML says 95/96 net lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   173.1   vs     308.4</p>
<p>    Gross sales		6,189.1   vs   5,122.8</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)		4.18  vs	 7.44</p>
<p>    Other income		131.5    vs	78.4</p>
<p>    Total expenditure     5,761.5    vs   4,652.5</p>
<p>    Interest costs	    164.5    vs     128.3</p>
<p>    Depreciation		109.5    vs     112.0</p>
<p>    Tax			    16.2    vs	 -</p>
<p>NOTE: Two-wheeler maker LML Ltd said it wrote-off 95.8 million rupees in 1995/96 (October-September) which was considered non-recoverable.</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
